<title>USA: Koch Oil cuts US posted crude oil prices 25 cts.</title>
<headline>Koch Oil cuts US posted crude oil prices 25 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective Thursday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $19.25 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $18.75 and Oklahoma sweet is $19.25.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
